/* NEW DRAFTS · Studio › AI Designer "Stitch" (9 Sep 2026) · shared data, the modular blocks and the phone screens.
   Plan: plans/studio-designer.md (§12 carries the owner's go decisions). Web screens and the board registration live in
   mod-studio-web.jsx. Everything renders through the theme object T (FINAL / FINALD); names are prefixed St… / ST_.
   Reuses from the base files: frameF, scrimF, Hit, Ic, glass, veil, smoke, Orb, AgentMark, PriceF, Meta, Mono, Num, Pill,
   Sect, OutBtn, Sheet, Body, DSearch, Thumb, LineG, Line, ViewTabs, RightPane, WebShell3, SheetBody, SheetFoot, ModeSwitch.

   THE STITCH WINDOW. The owner asked for "deep space black and white contrast" so the designer reads as agentic. Stitch's
   window (chat column + canvas) sits on a cool near-black (SP), white type, hairlines at 8 % white; the ERP chrome around it
   (rail, header, right pane, every other Studio screen) stays sand / espresso. Maroon remains the one accent line inside the
   window (send, active zone, current version). Stitch's personality is kept subtle, like the voice button: no avatar, no
   emoji. Stitch speaks in the display face; a spectral thread (the listening aura's colours) runs beside its words and
   under the stage while it draws; the orb breathes on the window head.

   MODULAR. One block per part, the same block on web and phone: StChat · StCanvas · StStrip · StTray · StPane (set / zone /
   version) · StTuner · StSwipe · StTile · StSwatch · StSeg · StSlider · StToggle. Web docks them; the phone stacks or sheets
   them. The renders on the stage are the owner's own ChatGPT output (assets/studio/), cut into tiles. */

